{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117099","id":3358144125,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7IKTZ9","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117099","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117099.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117099.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117099","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117099/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117099/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117099/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/794a002d4f65a7dd11a818cb52e4222237733f34","number":117099,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Use `uint32_t` and `int32_t` in the `RingBuffer`","user":{"login":"Brogolem35","id":29329606,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MzI5NjA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29329606?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35","html_url":"https://github.com/Brogolem35","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Unlike other generic containers of the core, RingBuffer has been using plain `int`s instead of `(u)int*_t`s or aliases to them. This PR attempts to modernize both the internals and the public APIs of the `RingBuffer` by using `(u)int*_t`s.\r\n\r\n## Known issues\r\nThe changes made in this PR seem to have a performance regression but I am not sure if it stems from my benchmarking method or uints having characteristics that I don't know of. Please let me know if I there is something wrong with my method.\r\n\r\nEdit: This regression seem to happen on GCC but not on Clang (didn't test MSVC). From what I understood from digging around the assembly is that, while GCC unrolls the loops with the `int` variant, it does not with the `uint32_t`. Clang doesn't seem to have this issue.\r\n\r\n### Benchmark code and method\r\nReplace `platform/linuxbsd/godot_linuxbsd.cpp` with the following and create a release build:\r\n```cpp\r\n#include \"os_linuxbsd.h\"\r\n\r\n#include \"core/profiling/profiling.h\"\r\n#include \"core/templates/ring_buffer.h\"\r\n#include \"main/main.h\"\r\n\r\n#ifdef _WIN32\r\n#include <intrin.h>\r\n#else\r\n#include <x86intrin.h>\r\n#endif\r\n\r\n#include <unistd.h>\r\n#include <climits>\r\n#include <clocale>\r\n#include <cstdlib>\r\n#include <iostream>\r\n\r\n#if defined(ASAN_ENABLED)\r\n#include <sys/resource.h>\r\n#endif\r\n\r\n#if defined(__x86_64) || defined(__x86_64__)\r\nvoid __cpuid(int *r_cpuinfo, int p_info) {\r\n\t// Note: Some compilers have a buggy `__cpuid` intrinsic, using inline assembly (based on LLVM-20 implementation) instead.\r\n\t__asm__ __volatile__(\r\n\t\t\t\"xchgq %%rbx, %q1;\"\r\n\t\t\t\"cpuid;\"\r\n\t\t\t\"xchgq %%rbx, %q1;\"\r\n\t\t\t: \"=a\"(r_cpuinfo[0]), \"=r\"(r_cpuinfo[1]), \"=c\"(r_cpuinfo[2]), \"=d\"(r_cpuinfo[3])\r\n\t\t\t: \"0\"(p_info));\r\n}\r\n#endif\r\n\r\n// For export templates, add a section; the exporter will patch it to enclose\r\n// the data appended to the executable (bundled PCK).\r\n#if !defined(TOOLS_ENABLED) && defined(__GNUC__)\r\nstatic const char dummy[8] __attribute__((section(\"pck\"), used)) = { 0 };\r\n\r\n// Dummy function to prevent LTO from discarding \"pck\" section.\r\nextern \"C\" const char *pck_section_dummy_call() __attribute__((used));\r\nextern \"C\" const char *pck_section_dummy_call() {\r\n\treturn &dummy[0];\r\n}\r\n#endif\r\n\r\nunsigned int _IA32_TSC_AUX;\r\nvolatile size_t volatile_size_t = 0;\r\n[[gnu::noipa]]\r\n__attribute__((noinline)) void black_box_write(RingBuffer<uint32_t> &set, Vector<uint32_t> &arr) {\r\n\tset.write(arr.ptr(), arr.size());\r\n}\r\n[[gnu::noipa]]\r\n__attribute__((noinline)) void black_box_single_read(RingBuffer<uint32_t> &set) {\r\n\tvolatile_size_t += set.read();\r\n}\r\n[[gnu::noipa]]\r\n__attribute__((noinline)) void black_box_array_read(RingBuffer<uint32_t> &set, Vector<uint32_t> &arr) {\r\n\tvolatile_size_t += set.read(arr.ptrw(), arr.capacity());\r\n}\r\n[[gnu::noipa]]\r\n__attribute__((noinline)) void black_box_clear(RingBuffer<uint32_t> &set) {\r\n\tset.clear();\r\n}\r\n\r\nint main(int argc, char *argv[]) {\r\n\tint cpuinfo[4];\r\n\tconstexpr int run_len = 20000;\r\n\r\n\tfor (const int size : { 1, 2, 8, 64, 1024, 4096, 20000 }) {\r\n\t\tstd::cout << \"RingBuffer<uint32_t>\" << size << std::endl;\r\n\t\t{\r\n\t\t\tsize_t time_ns = 0;\r\n\t\t\tsize_t time_ns1 = 0;\r\n\t\t\tfor (int run = 0; run < run_len / size; run++) {\r\n\t\t\t\tRingBuffer<uint32_t> set = { 20 };\r\n\t\t\t\tVector<uint32_t> tmp = {};\r\n\t\t\t\tfor (int idx = 0; idx < size; idx++) {\r\n\t\t\t\t\ttmp.append(idx);\r\n\t\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t\t\t__cpuid(cpuinfo, 0);\r\n\t\t\t\tauto t0 = __rdtsc();\r\n\t\t\t\tblack_box_write(set, tmp);\r\n\t\t\t\tauto t1 = __rdtscp(&_IA32_TSC_AUX);\r\n\t\t\t\t__cpuid(cpuinfo, 0);\r\n\t\t\t\ttime_ns += t1 - t0;\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\r\n\t\t\tstd::cout << \"write:\" << size << std::endl;\r\n\t\t\tstd::cout << time_ns << \"\\n\";\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\t{\r\n\t\t\tsize_t time_ns = 0;\r\n\t\t\tfor (int run = 0; run < run_len / size; run++) {\r\n\t\t\t\tRingBuffer<uint32_t> set = { 20 };\r\n\t\t\t\tfor (int idx = 0; idx < size; idx++) {\r\n\t\t\t\t\t// Test\r\n\t\t\t\t\tset.write(idx);\r\n\t\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t\t\tfor (int idx = 0; idx < size; idx++) {\r\n\t\t\t\t\t// Test\r\n\t\t\t\t\t__cpuid(cpuinfo, 0);\r\n\t\t\t\t\tauto t0 = __rdtsc();\r\n\t\t\t\t\tblack_box_single_read(set);\r\n\t\t\t\t\tauto t1 = __rdtscp(&_IA32_TSC_AUX);\r\n\t\t\t\t\t__cpuid(cpuinfo, 0);\r\n\t\t\t\t\ttime_ns += t1 - t0;\r\n\t\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\r\n\t\t\tstd::cout << \"single read:\" << size << std::endl;\r\n\t\t\tstd::cout << time_ns << \"\\n\";\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\t{\r\n\t\t\tsize_t time_ns = 0;\r\n\t\t\tfor (int run = 0; run < run_len / size; run++) {\r\n\t\t\t\tRingBuffer<uint32_t> set = { 20 };\r\n\t\t\t\tVector<uint32_t> tmp = {};\r\n\t\t\t\ttmp.reserve(size);\r\n\t\t\t\tfor (int idx = 0; idx < size; idx++) {\r\n\t\t\t\t\tset.write(idx);\r\n\t\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t\t\t__cpuid(cpuinfo, 0);\r\n\t\t\t\tauto t0 = __rdtsc();\r\n\t\t\t\tblack_box_array_read(set, tmp);\r\n\t\t\t\tauto t1 = __rdtscp(&_IA32_TSC_AUX);\r\n\t\t\t\t__cpuid(cpuinfo, 0);\r\n\t\t\t\ttime_ns += t1 - t0;\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\r\n\t\t\tstd::cout << \"array read:\" << size << std::endl;\r\n\t\t\tstd::cout << time_ns << \"\\n\";\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\t{\r\n\t\t\tsize_t time_ns = 0;\r\n\t\t\tfor (int run = 0; run < run_len / size; run++) {\r\n\t\t\t\tRingBuffer<uint32_t> set = { 20 };\r\n\t\t\t\tfor (int idx = 0; idx < size; idx++) {\r\n\t\t\t\t\t// Test\r\n\t\t\t\t\tset.write(idx);\r\n\t\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t\t\t__cpuid(cpuinfo, 0);\r\n\t\t\t\tauto t0 = __rdtsc();\r\n\t\t\t\tblack_box_clear(set);\r\n\t\t\t\tauto t1 = __rdtscp(&_IA32_TSC_AUX);\r\n\t\t\t\t__cpuid(cpuinfo, 0);\r\n\t\t\t\ttime_ns += t1 - t0;\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\r\n\t\t\tstd::cout << \"clear:\" << size << std::endl;\r\n\t\t\tstd::cout << time_ns << \"\\n\";\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t}\r\n}\r\n```\r\nYou can learn more about the use of `__cpuid`, `__rdtsc`, and `__rdtscp` at the [How to Benchmark Code Execution Times on Intel® IA-32 and IA-64 Instruction Set Architectures](https://cis.temple.edu/~qzeng/cis3207-spring18/files/ia-32-ia-64-benchmark-code-execution-paper.pdf) paper.\r\n\r\n### My results\r\n[old.log](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25765146/old.log)\r\n[new.log](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25765145/new.log)\r\n\r\n### My specs\r\nOS: Linux 6.18.13-arch1-1\r\nCPU: AMD Ryzen 7 PRO 4750G (16) @ 4.46 GHz\r\nGPU: AMD Radeon RX 6700 XT\r\nRAM: F4-3200C16D-32GVK","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097162,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTcxNjI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/discussion","name":"discussion","description":"","color":"ccaaff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":311852125,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMTE4NTIxMjU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/needs%20work","name":"needs work","description":"","color":"cc9999","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":410064485,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw0MTAwNjQ0ODU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/needs%20testing","name":"needs testing","description":"","color":"ffcc44","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creato